	(text "POWER MUX - powerboard has priority over USB.\nTPS2116 MODE tied to VIN1 = priority mode (TI SLVSFG1A sec 7.6.1); VREF(PR1) = 1.00V typ, 1.08V max.\n  U1 (5V):   VIN1 = +5V_PB,  VIN2 = VBUS.       PR1 divider R1/R2 = 100k/33k -> switchover at 4.03V\n  U2 (3V3):  VIN1 = +3V3_PB, VIN2 = +3V3_LDO.   PR1 divider R3/R4 = 100k/68k -> switchover at 2.47V\nWith the powerboard present, PR1 > VREF so VIN1 (powerboard) is selected. With USB only,\n+5V_PB/+3V3_PB = 0V so PR1 < VREF and the mux falls back to VBUS / the LDO.\n\nMARGIN AT THE RATED LOAD (5V @ 1A, 3V3 @ 1.5A), worst case against the 1.08V max VREF:\n  5V  @ 1.0A: drop = 1.0 x (0.100 FET + 0.020 fuse) = 0.120V -> rail 4.880V -> V(PR1) = 1.211V  (+12%)\n  3V3 @ 1.5A: drop = 1.5 x (0.100 FET + 0.015 fuse) = 0.173V -> rail 3.128V -> V(PR1) = 1.266V  (+17%)\n\nR45 (100k, VBUS->GND) is a bleeder. With no USB cable inserted VBUS is an open circuit,\nleaving U1 VIN2 and the U3 input floating; the bleeder defines them at 0V. Cost is 50 uA.\nC1 / C2 / C7 are the mux input decouplers - C1 on +5V_PB (U1 VIN1), C2 on VBUS (U1 VIN2),\nC7 on +3V3_PB (U2 VIN1). Each is drawn on the node it decouples, not hung off a bare label.\n\nCAUTION - USB-only operation is for BENCH PROGRAMMING, not full operation:\nU3 (TLV1117-33) is 800 mA and dissipates (5.0-3.3) x I = 1.4 W at 800 mA.\nThe radio module alone draws 650 mA on +3V3, plus ~330 mA on +5V for LEDs/OLED.\nThat exceeds both a default USB port and U3's comfortable dissipation."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 33.02 279.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "2a565227-375a-4add-939d-78bbbafbb28c")
	)
	(text "PR1 divider R1/R2\n100k/33k -> 4.03V"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 154.94 107.95 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "41236ea3-1472-42ac-a378-0605b434ac50")
	)
	(text "LIMITS / DESIGN NOTES\n1. D9 TVS0500 is a FLAT CLAMP (6.0V), chosen because TPS2116 abs max VIN is 6.0V.\n   A plain SMAJ6.0A clamps at 10.3V and would NOT have protected the mux.\n2. D10 on the 3V3 rail is transient/ESD only. No flat-clamp part exists below 5V Vrwm,\n   and SMAJ4.0CA does not conduct until 4.44V while STM32 VDD abs max is 4.0V.\n   A SUSTAINED 3V3 overvoltage is therefore NOT protected; the fuse trips on overcurrent\n   only. Upgrade path: active OVP load switch (TPS2595 / NCP360) in place of F3/Q2.\n3. R4 = 68k, not 56k. The series drop lowers +3V3_PB, and a 100k/56k divider leaves only\n   +4% over the 1.08V max VREF at the 1.5A rating, so the mux could falsely declare the\n   powerboard rail dead. 100k/68k restores it to +17%.\n4. Series drop budget per rail: P-FET 70-100 mOhm + fuse 15-20 mOhm."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 156.21 252.73 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "543133a3-9bc9-4a4a-af92-381338c7d171")
	)
	(text "R45 = VBUS bleeder\nVBUS floats with no\nUSB cable inserted"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 185.42 127 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "741638c9-705f-4d39-ac0b-20762cd71018")
	)
	(text "INPUT PROTECTION (powerboard connector J1 - JST-XH 6-way, friction lock)\nEach rail: fuse -> P-FET reverse-polarity -> TVS, emerging as +5V_PB / +3V3_PB.\nQ1/Q2 orientation: DRAIN->input, SOURCE->load, GATE->GND via 100k (R43/R44).\nA reversed supply reverse-biases the body diode AND drives Vgs to 0 => blocked.\nD11/D12 (10V zener, K->source, A->gate) clamp Vgs. In normal conduction Vgs = -Vin\nand the AO3401A abs max is +/-20V, so a miswired high supply would otherwise punch\nthrough the gate oxide. R43/R44 double as the zener current limit, (Vin-10V)/100k.\nEach TVS sits AFTER its FET, so it never sees a reversed input.\nF2/F3 are REGULAR fuses, NOT PTCs. A PTC's hold current derates to ~75% at 50C\nand ~50% at 70C: a 1.1A PTC on the 1A 5V rail holds only 0.83A at 50C and would\nnuisance-trip in a hot robot. A PTC is also 50-100 mOhm and rises after every\ntrip, against 15-20 mOhm stable for a fuse - and that series R sets the mux margin."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 156.21 279.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "8a2b5f17-bc57-4bf4-83a0-bdea060c3600")
	)
	(text "PR1 divider R3/R4\n100k/68k -> 2.47V"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 154.94 207.01 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "95a57186-e715-4bb5-b6d8-484c7245cc26")
	)
	(text "D11/D12: 10V Vgs clamp\n(AO3401A Vgs max +/-20V)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 124.46 85.09 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "fdecc146-108e-448b-9522-ebca0f37b186")
	)
